.TH start-cli-server-bittorrent-set-gua-wan 1  "set-gua-wan "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-server\-bittorrent\-set\-gua\-wan \- Expose an IPv6 global\-unicast address to the WAN (or revert it to LAN\-only) for a binding
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli server bittorrent set\-gua\-wan\fR <\fB\-\-address\fR> <\fB\-\-wan\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Expose an IPv6 global\-unicast address to the WAN (or revert it to LAN\-only) for a binding
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-address\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
Address details as a JSON HostnameInfo object
.TP
\fB\-\-wan\fR \fI<WAN>\fR
Expose the IPv6 GUA to the WAN (false = LAN\-only)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
